roaches 0 of f(x+h)/h','A',1,'2026-07-23 05:10:37','The derivative is defined as the limit of the difference quotient as h approaches 0.','MCQ',NULL),(47,22,'Using the power rule, what is the derivative of f(x) = x^4?','4x^3','x^5','4x^4','4x^2','A',1,'2026-07-23 05:10:37','The power rule states that the derivative of x^n is n*x^(n-1), so 4x^3 is correct.','MCQ',NULL),(48,22,'What is the derivative of the constant function f(x) = 7?','0','7','1','7x','A',1,'2026-07-23 05:10:37','The derivative of any constant is zero because constants have no rate of change.','MCQ',NULL),(49,22,'If f(x) = 3x^2 + 5x, what is f\'(x)?','6x + 5','3x + 5','6x^2 + 5x','3x^2 + 5','A',1,'2026-07-23 05:10:37','Applying the power rule and sum rule, the derivative of 3x^2 is 6x and 5x is 5.','MCQ',NULL),(50,22,'What is the derivative of f(x) = x^3 * x^2?','5x^4','3x^2 + 2x','x^5','6x^4','A',1,'2026-07-23 05:10:37','Simplifying first as x^5 gives 5x^4, but using the product rule also yields 5x^4.','MCQ',NULL),(51,23,'What is the indefinite integral of 3x^2?','x^3 + C','3x^3 + C','x^2 + C','3x + C','A',1,'2026-07-23 06:12:32','Integrating 3x^2 raises the exponent by one and divides by the new exponent.','MCQ',NULL),(52,23,'Which function is an antiderivative of sin x?','cos x + C','-cos x + C','sin x + C','-sin x + C','B',1,'2026-07-23 06:12:32','The derivative of -cos x is sin x, so its antiderivative of sin x is -cos x.','MCQ',NULL),(53,23,'Evaluate the indefinite integral ∫ (2x + 5) dx.','x^2 + 5x + C','2x^2 + 5x + C','x^2 + 5 + C','2x + 5 + C','A',1,'2026-07-23 06:12:32','Integrate term‑wise: ∫2x dx = x^2 and ∫5 dx = 5x.','MCQ',NULL),(54,23,'What is the value of the definite integral ∫_0^1 x^2 dx?','1/3','1/2','2/3','1','A',1,'2026-07-23 06:12:32','Applying the power rule gives [x^3/3]_0^1 = 1/3.','MCQ',NULL),(55,23,'Which integral yields a logarithmic function?','∫ 1/x dx','∫ x dx','∫ x^2 dx','∫ e^x dx','A',1,'2026-07-23 06:12:32','The antiderivative of 1/x is ln|x| + C, a logarithmic function.','MCQ',NULL),(56,24,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','Coal','Natural Gas','Solar Power','Nuclear Energy','C',1,'2026-07-23 09:10:11','Solar power is renewable because it is derived from sunlight, which is continuously replenished by the sun. Coal, natural gas, and nuclear energy are non-renewable as they rely on finite resources.','MCQ',NULL),(57,24,'What is the primary function of the heart in the human body?','To filter blood','To pump blood','To store oxygen','To produce hormones','B',1,'2026-07-23 09:10:11','The heart\'s main role is to pump blood throughout the circulatory system to deliver oxygen and nutrients to tissues. Blood filtration occurs in the kidneys, oxygen storage in muscle cells, and hormone production primarily in endocrine glands.','MCQ',NULL),(58,25,'Which political system is characterized by a single party controlling the state?','Democracy','Oligarchy','One-party state','Federalism','C',1,'2026-07-24 07:58:51','A one-party state is a government where only one political party is permitted to hold power, eliminating multiparty competition.','MCQ',NULL),(59,25,'What is the primary purpose of a constitution?','To declare war','To establish the framework of government','To collect taxes','To conduct elections','B',1,'2026-07-24 07:58:51','A constitution outlines the structure, powers, and limitations of government institutions and defines the rights of citizens.','MCQ',NULL),(60,25,'Which theory advocates for the abolition of private property?','Capitalism','Socialism','Communism','Libertarianism','C',1,'2026-07-24 07:58:51','Communism, as theorized by Marx, envisions a classless society where all property is communally owned, eliminating private ownership.','MCQ',NULL),(61,25,'What does the term \'separation of powers\' refer to?','Dividing a country into states','Splitting government into branches','Allowing multiple parties to govern','Reducing the power of the judiciary','B',1,'2026-07-24 07:58:51','Separation of 