ial explicitly states \'Problem 1 Classes Java code\' indicating that Problem 1 is about Classes and Java code.','MCQ',NULL),(296,84,'What does the output reference \'3 OP ABOVE\' in Problem 3 indicate?','The output is the number 3 from Problem 3 itself','The output references 3 lines of code above','The output refers to the result from Problem 2\'s output above','The output is unrelated to previous problems','C',1,'2026-07-28 11:33:44','The phrase \'OUTPUT: 3 OP ABOVE\' in Problem 3 indicates that the output refers to the result from the output of the problem above it (Problem 2).','MCQ',NULL),(297,85,'Which problem includes Classes Java code?','Problem 1','Problem 2','Problem 3','Problem 4','A',1,'2026-07-28 11:34:18','The study material states that Problem 1 contains Classes Java code.','MCQ',NULL),(298,85,'Which problem\'s output is given as 3?','Problem 1','Problem 2','Problem 3','Problem 4','C',1,'2026-07-28 11:34:18','The material shows OUTPUT: 3 associated with Problem 3.','MCQ',NULL),(299,85,'Which problem is referenced with the tag \'op:\'?','Problem 1','Problem 2','Problem 3','Problem 4','B',1,'2026-07-28 11:34:18','The material uses \'op:\' to denote Problem 2.','MCQ',NULL),(300,85,'Which problem is indicated to have an output above?','Problem 1','Problem 2','Problem 3','Problem 4','D',1,'2026-07-28 11:34:18','The phrase \'OP ABOVE: Problem 4: OUTPUT:\' points to Problem 4.','MCQ',NULL),(301,90,'What is the primary application of AI in addressing the Banana Problem in sustainable agriculture?','Automated harvesting of bananas','Disease detection in banana plants','Soil pH monitoring','Weather forecasting','B',1,'2026-07-28 12:26:47','AI is widely used in agriculture for identifying diseases in crops like bananas through image recognition and machine learning models, enabling early intervention and sustainable practices.','MCQ',NULL),(302,90,'Which machine learning technique is most commonly employed for classifying banana leaf diseases?','Support Vector Machines (SVM)','Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN)','Random Forest','K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)','B',1,'2026-07-28 12:26:47','CNNs are specialized for image processing and are extensively used in agricultural AI to analyze visual data, such as banana leaf images, for accurate disease classification.','MCQ',NULL),(303,90,'What is a key benefit of integrating AI in banana farming for sustainable development?','Increased dependency on chemical fertilizers','Reduction in pesticide usage','Higher labor costs','Slower crop monitoring','B',1,'2026-07-28 12:26:47','AI enables precise disease detection and targeted treatment, reducing the need for excessive chemical pesticides and promoting environmentally sustainable farming practices.','MCQ',NULL),(304,90,'What type of data is critical for training AI models to detect banana plant diseases?','Historical rainfall data','Images of infected banana leaves','Market price trends','GPS coordinates of farms','B',1,'2026-07-28 12:26:47','Visual data, such as images of diseased leaves, is essential for training AI models to identify patterns and symptoms associated with specific banana plant diseases.','MCQ',NULL),(305,91,'What is the primary subject matter mentioned in the provided study material?','AI for Sustainable Development','Banana Problem Name','Trishul Swamy','Unit-3 HM SRN','A',1,'2026-07-28 12:28:15','The study material explicitly states \'AI FOR SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT\' at the beginning.','MCQ',NULL),(306,91,'Which unit is the study material associated with?','Unit-1','Unit-2','Unit-3','Unit-4','C',1,'2026-07-28 12:28:15','The material specifies \'UNIT-3\'.','MCQ',NULL),(307,91,'What name is associated with the \'Banana Problem\' in the text?','Trishul Swamy','PES1UG23CS658','HM SRN','SEC:K','A',1,'2026-07-28 12:28:15','The material lists \'BANANA PROBLEM NAME :Trishul Swamy\'.','MCQ',NULL),(308,91,'What is the student\'s SRN according to the document?','PES1UG23CS658','TRISHUL123','BANANA-01','UNIT-3-HM','A',1,'2026-07-28 12:28:15','The material lists \'SRN:PES1UG23CS658\'.','MCQ',NULL),(309,92,'What is the required team size for the Mini-Project according to the guidelines?','2 members','3 members','4 members','5 members','C',1,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','The guidelines explicitly state: \'The students have to form a team of 4 members\'.','MCQ',NULL),(310,92,'Which type of application is explicitly NOT accepted for this project?','Web applications','Desktop applications','Mobile applications','Java Swing applications','C',1,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','The guidelines state: \'However, only Desktop and Web applications are accepted. Mobile applications are not accepted.\'','MCQ',NULL),(311,92,'In the marks distribution, how many marks are allocated to the Activity Diagram?','1 mark','2 marks','4 marks','3 marks','C',1,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','The marks distribution specifies: \'Activity Diagram – 4\'.','MCQ',NULL),(312,92,'How many design patterns must a 4-member team include (excluding the one enforced by the framework)?','2 patterns','3 patterns','4 patterns','1 pattern','C',1,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','The note states: \'4 Design patterns (should contain Creational, Structural and Behavioral Patterns apart from one enforced by the framework)\'.','MCQ',NULL),(313,92,'According to the guidelines, how should a student\'s ownership of a use case be structured?','One student owns the UI and another owns the Backend','Each student should own a use case completely and implement it','The team shares a single use case equally','The Administrator owns all use cases','B',1,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','The guidelines state: \'Each student should own a use case completely and implement it (that is, avoid situations where a team member will own only UI, another will own Backend etc.)\'.','MCQ',NULL),(314,92,'What is the deadline for submitting the Mini-project specifications in Phase 1?','Week 15','23rd Jan 2026','End of semester','Week 14','B',1,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','Phase 1 deadline is explicitly stated as \'23 rd Jan 2026\'.','MCQ',NULL),(315,92,'Based on the Library Management Software sample, describe the different roles/users in the system and their primary responsibilities.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','The answer covers all three roles mentioned in the sample specifications: Members, Librarians, and Administrators.','DESCRIPTIVE','The system supports three user types: \n1. Members: They search for books using criteria like title, author, or category, view availability, borrow books (after verification), and return books (updating availability and paying fines).\n2. Librarians: They manage the library catalog (add, update, remove books), manage member records, and calculate fines for overdue returns.\n3. Administrators: They oversee user management, manage librarian accounts, generate usage reports, and monitor system performance.'),(316,92,'List the required components that must be included in the final Report document.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 12:31:51','This list is directly extracted from the \'Submission\' section of the study material.','DESCRIPTIVE','The report must include:\n- Title page (Course details, project title, team members using PESU template)\n- Problem statement (synopsis)\n- Models (Use Case, Class Models, Activity Diagrams, State Diagrams)\n- Architecture Patterns, Design Principles and Design Patterns used with short descriptions of application\n- Github link to the public/accessible codebase\n- Individual contributions of team members\n- Screenshots with input values and output shown (using white background screens)'),(317,93,'What is the required team size for the mini-project?','3 members','4 members','5 members','6 members','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The study material explicitly states that a team of 4 members is required.','MCQ',NULL),(318,93,'Which of the following is NOT part of the evaluation criteria for analysis and design models?','Use Case Diagram','Class Diagram','Agile Methodology','State Diagram','C',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The evaluation criteria include Use Case, Class, Activity, and State diagrams, but not Agile Methodology.','MCQ',NULL),(319,93,'Which framework is mandatory for MVC implementation in this project?','Java Spring Framework','Hibernate','Struts','JavaFX','A',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The study material specifies the use of Java Spring Framework (or similar MVC frameworks) for implementation.','MCQ',NULL),(320,93,'How many design patterns are required in total for a 4-member team?','3 patterns','4 patterns','5 patterns','6 patterns','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The note specifies that 4 design patterns (creational, structural, behavioral, and one enforced by the framework) are required.','MCQ',NULL),(321,93,'What must each student own in terms of use cases?','UI components','Backend logic','A complete use case','Database management','C',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The material emphasizes that each student should own a use case entirely to avoid role-based division.','MCQ',NULL),(322,93,'Which of the following diagrams is NOT required in the analysis and design phase?','Use Case Diagram','Sequence Diagram','Activity Diagram','Class Diagram','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The required diagrams are Use Case, Class, Activity, and State diagrams, as per the marks distribution.','MCQ',NULL),(323,93,'What is the deadline for Phase 1 submission?','15th Jan 2026','23rd Jan 2026','1st Feb 2026','15th Feb 2026','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','Phase 1 requires submission of specifications by 23rd Jan 2026, as stated in the material.','MCQ',NULL),(324,93,'Which of the following is a mandatory requirement for data handling?','Use of in-memory storage','Data persistence in a database','No database required','Cloud-based storage only','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The study material mandates that data must be persisted in a chosen database.','MCQ',NULL),(325,93,'Explain how you would apply at least one design principle and one design pattern in your project, specifying their roles and benefits.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The answer should link the principle/pattern to the project\'s requirements, such as managing library resources or user roles.','DESCRIPTIVE','A design principle like \'Single Responsibility\' ensures each class handles one task, reducing complexity. A design pattern like \'Singleton\' could manage a single instance of a database connection, ensuring consistency and efficient resource use.'),(326,93,'Describe the MVC architecture implementation in this project, including how each component (Model, View, Controller) is utilized for different user roles.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The answer must detail MVC components\' roles in handling user-specific functionalities as per the project\'s requirements.','DESCRIPTIVE','The Model handles data and business logic (e.g., book availability checks), the View manages UI for user interactions (e.g., book search forms), and the Controller processes requests (e.g., issuing books based on member roles). Roles like librarians and administrators would have distinct controllers to enforce access control.'),(327,93,'Discuss the importance of data persistence in the library management system and how it should be implemented using a chosen database.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 13:00:05','The answer should emphasize how persistence supports critical functionalities like tracking book status and user interactions.','DESCRIPTIVE','Data persistence ensures accurate records of books, users, and transactions. A relational database like MySQL could store tables for Books, Members, and Transactions, with foreign keys to maintain relationships. This prevents data loss and supports features like overdue fines and book availability checks.'),(328,94,'What is the title of the unit?','AI FOR SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT','BANANA PROBLEM','UNIT-3','PART2','A',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:03','The study material begins with the title \'AI FOR SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT\' indicating the subject of the unit.','MCQ',NULL),(329,94,'Which unit number is referenced?','Unit-1','Unit-2','Unit-3','Unit-4','C',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:03','The study material explicitly mentions \'UNIT-3\' as the unit number.','MCQ',NULL),(330,94,'What is the name of the problem discussed?','Apple Problem','Banana Problem','Cherry Problem','Date Problem','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:03','The study material states the problem name as \'BANANA PROBLEM\'.','MCQ',NULL),(331,94,'Who is the student name?','Trishul Swamy','Rohan Patel','Anita Desai','Vikram Singh','A',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','The study material provides the student\'s name as \'Trishul Swamy\'.','MCQ',NULL),(332,94,'What is the SRN?','PES1UG23CS658','PES1UG22CS658','PES1UG23CS659','PES1UG23CS657','A',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','The SRN is directly given as \'PES1UG23CS658\' in the study material.','MCQ',NULL),(333,94,'What section is mentioned?','Section A','Section B','Section K','Section L','C',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','The study material specifies the section as \'Section K\'.','MCQ',NULL),(334,94,'What part is indicated?','Part 1','Part 2','Part 3','Part 4','B',1,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','The study material ends with \'PART2\', indicating the part number.','MCQ',NULL),(335,94,'List all the information provided in the study material about the AI for Sustainable Development Unit-3 Banana Problem assignment.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','This answer enumerates each piece of information explicitly present in the provided study material.','DESCRIPTIVE','The study material includes: title \'AI FOR SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT\', unit number \'Unit-3\', problem name \'Banana Problem\', student name \'Trishul Swamy\', SRN \'PES1UG23CS658\', section \'Section K\', and part \'Part 2\'.'),(336,94,'What is the SRN of the student named Trishul Swamy in the given study material?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,3,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','The SRN is directly stated as \'PES1UG23CS658\' in the study material.','DESCRIPTIVE','PES1UG23CS658'),(337,94,'Identify the unit number and part number referenced in the study material.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4,'2026-07-28 13:35:04','The study material explicitly mentions \'UNIT-3\' and \'PART2\' as the unit and part numbers.','DESCRIPTIVE','Unit-3 and Part 2'),(338,95,'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of a blockchain network?','Decentralized','Immutable','Centralized','Transparent','C',1,'2026-07-28 15:02:50','Blockchain networks are inherently decentralized, meaning no single entity controls them. Centralization contradicts the core principle of blockchain technology.','MCQ',NULL),(339,95,'What is the primary purpose of a Merkle tree in blockchain technology?','To encrypt transaction data','To compress large datasets','To verify data integrity','To speed up transaction processing','C',1,'2026-07-28 15:02:50','A Merkle tree ensures data integrity by allowing efficient verification of transaction details through hashing. It does not encrypt or compress data.','MCQ',NULL),(340,95,'Which consensus mechanism is most energy-efficient for blockchain networks?','Proof of Work','Proof of Stake','Proof of Authority','Delegated Proof of Stake','B',1,'2026-07-28 15:02:50','Proof of Stake (PoS) consumes significantly less energy compared to Proof of Work (PoW), which requires intensive computational power for mining.','MCQ',NULL),(341,95,'What is a smart contract in the context of blockchain?','A legal agreement stored on paper','A self-executing contract with terms written in code','A type of blockchain node','A security protocol for data encryption','B',1,'2026-07-28 15:02:50','Smart contracts automatically execute actions when predefined conditions are met, eliminating the need for intermediaries.','MCQ',NULL),(342,95,'Explain the concept of gas fees in blockchain networks like Ethereum. How do they function and why are they necessary?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-28 15:02:50','Gas fees incentivize honest behavior by making users bear the cost of network usage. They ensure fair resource allocation and prevent abuse of the blockchain\'s computational power.','DESCRIPTIVE','Gas fees are transaction costs paid by users to compensate miners or validators for processing and validating transactions on a blockchain network. They function as a pricing mechanism to prevent spam and ensure network efficiency. Gas fees are calculated based on the computational effort required to execute a transaction or smart contract. Users set a gas limit and price, and the network allocates resources accordingly. Without gas fees, the network could be overwhelmed by malicious or excessive transactions, compromising its security and functionality.'),(343,96,'What condition occurs when processes form a circular wait for resources?','Deadlock','Starvation','Livelock','Thrashing','A',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','All involved processes are waiting for each other, preventing progress.','MCQ',NULL),(344,96,'When a high‑priority task is blocked by a lower‑priority task, what phenomenon can arise?','Priority inversion','Deadlock','Starvation','Convoy effect','A',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','The lower‑priority task holds a resource needed by the higher‑priority task.','MCQ',NULL),(345,96,'Which memory allocation method is most prone to external fragmentation?','Paging','Segmentation','Contiguous allocation','Buddy system','C',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','Free memory blocks are scattered, making them unusable for larger requests.','MCQ',NULL),(346,96,'Which page replacement algorithm replaces the page that will not be used for the longest time?','FIFO','LRU','Optimal','Clock','C',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','It requires future knowledge to achieve the lowest possible page faults.','MCQ',NULL),(347,96,'What is the first software component executed after the BIOS on a PC?','Bootloader','Kernel','System call interface','Device driver','A',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','It loads the operating system kernel into memory.','MCQ',NULL),(348,96,'Which hardware privilege level allows direct access to CPU instructions?','User mode','Kernel mode','Guest mode','Ring 3','B',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','Only kernel mode can execute privileged CPU instructions.','MCQ',NULL),(349,96,'In a multilevel feedback queue, how are processes moved between queues?','Based on their remaining burst time','According to priority aging','When they exceed time quantum','Randomly each scheduling round','C',1,'2026-07-29 02:56:11','Processes that use up their time slice are demoted to a lower‑priority queue.','MCQ',NULL),(350,97,'Which scheduling algorithm minimizes average waiting time for a set of processes with known burst times?','Shortest Job First','Round Robin','First-Come First-Served','Priority Scheduling','A',1,'2026-07-29 03:02:09','SJF is optimal for minimizing average waiting time when burst times are known.','MCQ',NULL),(351,97,'In a demand-paged virtual memory system, what does the \'working set\' model track?','Pages referenced in the last Δ time','Total pages allocated','Page fault frequency','Swap space usage','A',1,'2026-07-29 03:02:09','The working set is the set of pages a process has referenced in the recent window Δ.','MCQ',NULL),(352,97,'Which file system uses a copy-on-write mechanism for metadata updates?','ZFS','ext4','NTFS','FAT32','A',1,'2026-07-29 03:02:09','ZFS employs copy-on-write for both data and metadata to ensure consistency.','MCQ',NULL),(353,97,'What is the primary purpose of a \'spinlock\' in kernel synchronization?','Busy-wait for a short critical section','Block the thread until lock free','Allow multiple readers simultaneously','Prevent priority inversion','A',1,'2026-07-29 03:02:09','Spinlocks repeatedly test the lock, suitable for very short critical sections where sleeping overhead is higher.','MCQ',NULL),(354,97,'In a microkernel architecture, which service typically runs in user space?','Device drivers','Scheduler','Interrupt handler','Memory manager','A',1,'2026-07-29 03:02:09','Microkernels move device drivers, file systems, and networking to user-space processes.','MCQ',NULL),(355,98,'According to the course material, which of the following correctly pairs a parser generator tool with the parsing technique it primarily supports?','Lex – LR(0) parsing','Yacc/Bison – LALR parsing','Flex – LL(1) parsing','GNU Bison – LL(*) parsing','B',1,'2026-07-29 03:07:39','In the course, Yacc/Bison is introduced as a parser generator that constructs LALR parsers, while Lex/Flex is used for lexical analysis, not for LR(0) parsing. LL(1) parsing is associated with hand‑written predictive parsers, and LL(*) is a more advanced technique not covered as the primary output of Yacc/Bison in this curriculum.','MCQ',NULL),(356,99,'What does DUU stand for?','Down Under University','Data Usage Utility','Digital University Union','Diverse Undergraduate Unit','A',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material explicitly states that DUU stands for Down Under University.','MCQ',NULL),(357,99,'How many staff does Down Under University have?','5,000','7,000','10,000','50,000','B',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material states that DUU has 7,000 staff.','MCQ',NULL),(358,99,'How many students does Down Under University have?','7,000','14,000','50,000','140,000','C',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material states that DUU has 50,000 students.','MCQ',NULL),(359,99,'From how many countries do international students at DUU come?','Over 40 countries','Over 70 countries','Over 100 countries','Over 140 countries','D',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material states that international students come from over 140 countries.','MCQ',NULL),(360,99,'Which website hosts the Impact Rankings that DUU is compared on?','www.universityrankings.com','www.timeshighereducation.com/impactrankings','www.duu.edu.au/rankings','www.globaluniversityrankings.org','B',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material provides the URL https://www.timeshighereducation.com/impactrankings for exploring THE Impact Rankings.','MCQ',NULL),(361,99,'What type of study options does DUU offer?','Only undergraduate programmes','Only postgraduate programmes','Hundreds of undergraduate and postgraduate study options','Only research-based degrees','C',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material states that DUU offers hundreds of undergraduate and postgraduate study options.','MCQ',NULL),(362,99,'Which of the following is mentioned as a feature of DUU\'s academics?','Part-time visiting lecturers','Leading academics','Online-only faculty','Guest speakers from industry','B',1,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material describes DUU\'s academics as \'leading academics\'.','MCQ',NULL),(363,99,'What two key facilities or approaches does DUU highlight to deliver real-world outcomes for students and graduates?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material states that state-of-the-art teaching facilities and a focussed approach to learning deliver real-world outcomes for students and graduates.','DESCRIPTIVE','State-of-the-art teaching facilities and a focussed approach to learning.'),(364,99,'Describe the diversity of the student and staff community at Down Under University.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material provides specific details about the cultural and religious diversity of DUU\'s community, including numbers of staff, students, and countries represented.','DESCRIPTIVE','DUU\'s 7,000 staff and 50,000 students come from many different cultural and religious backgrounds, including international students from over 140 countries.'),(365,99,'What is the purpose of the Impact Rankings mentioned in the study material?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,'2026-07-29 03:13:15','The study material links the Impact Rankings to exploring higher education and comparing university performance on sustainability via THE (Times Higher Education).','DESCRIPTIVE','The Impact Rankings are used to explore higher education and compare university performance on sustainability.');
